{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/599415-government-hunters-and-lack-of-knowledge","id":599415,"title":"Government hunters, and lack of knowledge.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-22T08:12:43-07:00","id":599415,"title":"Government hunters, and lack of knowledge.","content":"Is it unrealistic, that government hunters, dont have huge databases, with comprehensive lists of tribes, and clans, since the PC's arent the first government hunters to come out<br /> <br /> had one player who was extremely miffed at that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T08:32:36-07:00","id":599441,"title":"","content":"They don't have that info. The only one who has info even close is Bob Schnoblin, and, well, he's Bob Schnoblin, who has clumsily organized these names into a &quot;Pyramid of Satanic Power&quot;. Anyone else who gets this info from him likely doesn't have a future career in Intelligence, so there you go. Government agencies aren't all-knowing, all-trusting affairs. They're nightmares of office politics, clearance levels, and pet projects, so even if a database existed, the PCs likely wouldn't be cleared for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T09:37:44-07:00","id":599510,"title":"","content":"Bob's attempts to explain everything appear in <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/235/Project-Twilight\" target=\"_blank\">Project Twilight</a>, which can provide you with a fairly well informed government hunting organisation. Ultimately, though, there are plenty of reasons for internal cover-ups, information not being forwarded and the like. As Saur Ops Specialist notes above, there are real-world explanations, and suitably paranoid 'conspiracy theory' explanations too.<br /> <br /> Look at how other settings deal with supernaturala nd paranormal staying secret while government agents look into it. There's a conspiracy constantly trying to shut <b>The X Files</b> down, while other conspiratorial forces work to keep it going. In Pagan Publishing's <b>Delta Green</b> setting, the hunters have to work off the books due to a conspiracy within the government working for &quot;the other side&quot; targeting their leaders and wiping out most of their intelligence network years ago, and it's still after them now. <b>Night's Black Agents</b> from Pelgrane Press looks at different approaches to spies fighting supernatural conspiracies, from well-informed and organised agencies waging a secret war for decades to the PCs literally being the first agents to discover the supernatural.<br /> <br /> It would be possible to tweak the setting so that there's a reliable well-informed government agency looking into the supernatural (the Technocracy from <b>Mage: The Ascension</b> already does this to an extent, while also actively suppressing the spread of information) but things being too open would change how it feels. The setting can also justify a clueless government, or one actively stonewalling attempts to break the silence, or one co-opted by the forces the players' characters have to fight. There are plenty of people - and other things - with an investment in keeping the supernatural secret. It may not be 100% realistic, but realism usually gives way to theme and premise in the <b>World Of Darkness</b> games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T23:00:45-07:00","id":600234,"title":"","content":"In the end, IRL explanations or Conspiratorial ones break down to a simple thing: no government works as a monolithic structure. They ARE fractured, for a lot of reasons.<br /> <br /> With that, information gets lost in the way in a daily basis. Sometimes it does exist somewhere, but it doesn't mean you have access to it. Other times it is just lost, by accident or interference. And yet others it never makes its way to the archives to begin with, for reasons.<br /> <br /> Think about how much one government can be infiltrated by Mages, Vampires, Werewolfs, Changelings, Hunters and Demons, and those guys working to mess with a system that doesn't even need help to be a mess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T17:11:13-07:00","id":602376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/599415-government-hunters-and-lack-of-knowledge#post599415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it unrealistic, that government hunters, dont have huge databases, with comprehensive lists of tribes, and clans, since the PC's arent the first government hunters to come out<br /> <br /> had one player who was extremely miffed at that.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do have huge databases with comprehensive lists.... that's the problem. Their lists include TOO MUCH. How do you sort fact from falsehood from insane cultist ramblings from movie script from confused recollection of a delirium-inflicted witness from reality? What do you corroborate it against?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T18:58:52-07:00","id":602422,"title":"","content":"And let's say an agent witnesses supernatural goings-on first hand. One of three things happens: 1) his superiors don't believe him, 2) someone in the know shuts him up one way or another, or 3) he doesn't say anything that would suggest paranormal activity, for the previous two reasons. Keep in mind that on X-Files, Fox Mulder had a basement office and no chance of promotion. Partly because of the ludicrousness of the cases he investigates, and partly because he's aggressive about his conspiracy theories. The only reason he wasn't fired or quietly silenced is because he has friends in Washington who would ask questions if anything happened to him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}